Documentation for comparator
----------------------------
rev 0.3, 7/16/99:   Added NAME_comparator proc, which creates the comparator 
                    name
rev 0.2, 6/14/99:   Added support for Operation and OutputAssertion parameters
rev 0.1, 6/11/99:   Initial release



The comparator generator is used to derive a circuit which detects exact 
equality between its two inputs, or to compare a single input to zero.


GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NBITS:
    Definition: 
      The number of bits in the input values A_H and B_H.
    Legal values:
      1 <= NBITS <= 128
    Default:
      32

  Operation:
    Definition:
      The operation to be performed by this generator:  comparison of
      two inputs, or zero detection on one input.
    Legal Values:
      Compare or ZeroDetect
    Default:
      Compare

  OutputAssertion:
    Definition:
      The desired assertion level of the output signal.  The user may
      select H (output is High (1) if the inputs are the same or if zero
      is detected), L (output is Low (0) if the inputs are the same), 
      or Both (both H and L signals are derived).
    Legal Values:
      H (high), L (low), or Both (two output signals driven)
    Default:
      H